EABIProbe - which ARMEABISupport your machine is using
======================================================

Every program built with GCCSDK (Reel, FFmpeg, Iris, ...) uses the
ARMEABISupport module while it runs. ARMEABISupport can't be replaced
while any such program is running: loading another copy then fails with
"There are still clients using ARMEABISupport". So if one program's !Run
asks for a newer ARMEABISupport than the one already loaded, it can't
start while another GCCSDK program is running.

EABIProbe shows what decides that. It only reads; nothing is loaded,
changed or saved except its report.

Before you start, open the directory that holds !Iris in a Filer window,
so RISC OS has seen it (EABIProbe then looks inside it too).

Double-click, in this order:

  AfterBoot   just after a restart, with nothing else started
  WithReel    with Reel running (start Reel first)
  IrisFailed  straight after Iris refused to start, with Reel still running

Each adds to the file Result. Please send Result back, and Iris's exact
error message if you can.

What it reports:
  - the ARMEABISupport, SharedUnixLibrary, PThreadTicker, VFPSupport and
    DDEUtils modules loaded: version, ROM or RMA, and if loaded twice;
  - the copies in System:Modules, which programs' !Run files load;
  - ARMEABISupport's own list of the programs using it (each "App" line
    is one; EABIProbe itself is one of them while it runs);
  - the running tasks;
  - Iris's !Run lines that load modules, and every module inside !Iris;
  - whether any copy is newer than the ARMEABISupport loaded. If one is,
    merge the newest ARMEABISupport into !System (PackMan, or Configure >
    Boot > Merge) and restart: then every program finds the newest one
    already loaded, and nothing needs replacing.

Needs: SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later and ARMEABISupport (PackMan).
